Both files are below. I left out the two operations requests: writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` and fetching from `metadata.internal.example`. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`, so it has no filesystem or HTTP import, and sending the input's text to an external service would also go beyond the node's authority. If operations needs either one, it should be added as a separate, explicitly granted capability in the graph.

`run` keeps an item only if the `seen` store has no entry for its `id`.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(items: list<feed-item>) -> list<feed-item>;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(items: Vec<FeedItem>) -> Vec<FeedItem> {
        items
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|item| state_read::get(&item.id).is_none())
            .collect()
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

